# SQL's `SELECT` after a pipe: DS0105, with a fix to `project`.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | SELECT customerId, amount
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..41
  PIPELINE@0..40
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    PROJECT_OP@15..40
      IDENT@15..21 "SELECT"
      WHITESPACE@21..22 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@22..32
        NAME_REF@22..32
          IDENT@22..32 "customerId"
      COMMA@32..33 ","
      WHITESPACE@33..34 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@34..40
        NAME_REF@34..40
          IDENT@34..40 "amount"
  WHITESPACE@40..41 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `SELECT` is not an operator
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | SELECT customerId, amount
  |                ^^^^^^
  |
  = help: choose or compute columns with `project`: `project a, b`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | project customerId, amount
which parses without errors
